---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <div class="strf-main-content">
    <section class="strf-section">
      <h1>Welcome to Storagefy</h1>
      <p>
        <strong>Storagefy</strong> is a unified adapter system for syncing your state
        management libraries (like <em>Pinia</em>, <em>Zustand</em>, <em
          >Redux</em
        >, <em>Svelte stores</em>, and more) with browser storage mechanisms
        like <strong>localStorage</strong>, <strong>sessionStorage</strong>, or <strong
          >IndexedDB</strong
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        It’s built to be <strong>framework-agnostic</strong>, lightweight, and
        highly composable — empowering you to persist your state across reloads
        and sessions in a clean, plug-and-play way.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="strf-section">
      <h2>Installation</h2>
      <pre class="strf-code-block"><code>npm install storagefy</code></pre>
      <p>Or with yarn:</p>
      <pre class="strf-code-block"><code>yarn add storagefy</code></pre>
      <p>The package ships its TypeScript declarations.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="strf-section">
      <h2>What's new in 1.3.0</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <code>keyDerivation</code>: <code>"hkdf"</code> (the new default, fast) or <code>"pbkdf2"</code> (slow on
          purpose, for a password the person types). Values written by 1.2.x are still read.
        </li>
        <li><code>onError</code> on reads: tell "nothing stored" from "stored but unreadable".</li>
        <li>
          Writes of a key land in the order they were made; IndexedDB reports a write saved only once its
          transaction is; a burst of changes to a store is one write.
        </li>
        <li>
          Fixed: Svelte stores now sync between tabs; several stores can share one storage adapter's channel;
          <code>list(prefix)</code> and <code>getAll(table)</code> filter; large values encrypt.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Read the
        <a href="https://github.com/arthurgermano/storagefy/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md">changelog</a> before upgrading:
        values written by 1.3.0 cannot be read by older versions.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="strf-section">
      <h2>About encryption</h2>
      <p>
        <code>encrypt: true</code> makes the stored values hard to read in the browser's tools. It does not keep a
        secret: everything needed to decrypt ships with your app. <strong>Never store tokens, passwords or personal
        data you must protect</strong> — keep Storagefy for preferences, carts, drafts and the like.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="strf-section">
      <h2>Adapters Overview</h2>

      <div class="strf-adapter">
        <h3>LocalStorageAdapter</h3>
        <p>
          Persists your state using the browser’s <code>localStorage</code>.
          Data survives across tabs and sessions. Great for most use cases that
          need durable client-side persistence.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="strf-adapter">
        <h3>SessionStorageAdapter</h3>
        <p>
          Uses <code>sessionStorage</code> for persistence that lasts only for the
          duration of the browser tab — for temporary state. It is gone when the tab closes, but it does not protect
          anything while the tab is open.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="strf-adapter">
        <h3>IndexedDBAdapter</h3>
        <p>
          Stores large and complex state structures asynchronously using
          IndexedDB — the default adapter. A write is reported saved only once its transaction is; the service worker
          of a PWA can read it too.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="strf-section">
      <h2>Stores Overview</h2>

      <div class="strf-adapter">
        <h3>React Store Adapter</h3>
        <p>
          Seamlessly syncs state from React-based stores like <strong
            >Redux</strong
          >, <strong>Zustand</strong>, <strong>Jotai</strong>, or custom hooks
          to any supported storage adapter. Built for flexibility, supporting
          both controlled and uncontrolled stores.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="strf-adapter">
        <h3>Svelte Store Adapter</h3>
        <p>
          Persists Svelte <code>writable</code> stores with minimal setup and keeps reactivity intact. Load what was
          kept with <code>getFromStorage</code>, then keep every change with <code>setInStorage</code>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="strf-adapter">
        <h3>Vue (Pinia) Store Adapter</h3>
        <p>
          Integrates with <strong>Pinia</strong> (Vue 3’s store library) to persist
          state across sessions. Easy to plug into existing Pinia stores, enabling
          persistence without side effects.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
